    [91206] = "Opens after the For Zul'Aman! achievement.",
    [91270] = "Any of the four team names works.",
    [91271] = "Fish from the special pool at the marker; it disappears when anyone fishes it and respawns slowly. If none shows, untrack and retrack the quest, or relog.",
    [91284] = "Take and finish one quest from each of the three mentors first; each then gives you their recommendation. The magister's one is charging a staff to the south-west.",
    [91292] = "Ignore the marker by the quest giver: the crystals are on the bridge to Silvermoon City, at 42.2, 20.4.",
    [91301] = "Instructor Thalendir is in Falconwing Square, Silvermoon City, at 33.2, 74.1.",
    [91339] = "The targets are around the outside of the hole and in a few nearby caves, not down the hole. Choosing to spare the younglings is allowed but costs you health.",
    [91340] = "The enemies are at ground level; don't go down yet.",
    [91341] = "Go down into the pit despite what the NPC says. Jump through the void energy above the spinning red blades; gravity is low in there.",
    [91343] = "The last quest of this storyline. If he vanishes when you attack, try taunting him.",
    [91346] = "Appears after the campaign quest Watch the Den.",
    [91347] = "If you can't mount a strider because several are stacked, wait for them to clear. If you're stuck mounted afterwards, run into the tree behind him and relog.",
    [91348] = "Click the faint green lotus-like flower next to the quest giver.",
    [91359] = "If no Feasting Lashrooms are left, relog to get some to spawn.",
    [91361] = "Needs more of the Harandar campaign done before it appears.",
    [91375] = "Needs the campaign quest Tell the People What You Have Seen before the chain can continue.",
    [91378] = "Few enemies with slow respawns; patience.",
    [91380] = "No need to go to Silvermoon: Fidoficus is right behind you. Click him to feed him.",
    [91382] = "You get Fidoficus as a pet whichever answer you choose; wait for him to finish talking before leaving.",
    [91385] = "If you can't click the NPC, move around; it may only respond from its right side near the back.",
    [91386] = "The items are on the ground floor of the building with the jewelcrafting trainer (48.9, 54.2); just drop down from the first floor. The chain rewards a curtain decor pattern.",
    [91388] = "Kill the Weakened enemy until it turns friendly, then use the quest item on it.",
    [91389] = "Gaari is at 45.1, 34.3.",
    [91406] = "Won't show its items while your zone campaign quest is active; finish the campaign first. The last clue is upstairs in the hut.",
    [91407] = "Dismount to see the extra action button.",
    [91409] = "Nothing to use from your bags: click the fang and the eye on two of the pillars.",
    [91411] = "The shell drops from the second boss of Maisara Caverns. The turn-in is underground; the entrance is at 39.7, 23.2.",
    [91426] = "If Arator isn't there to take it, fly away and come back.",
    [91452] = "Stand at each marked shelf until the extra action button appears, then press it to put the books back. If it won't show, reload, or macro /click ExtraActionButton1.",
    [91494] = "Use the item on the vial at your feet first, then on the mana wyrms and canisters.",
    [91533] = "The first quest of this storyline. Appears only after the campaign quest Daylight is Breaking.",
    [91537] = "Easy to miss: it's above the blue fire pit near Tracker Arieni.",
    [91545] = "The last quest of this storyline; it starts with What We Leave Behind.",
    [91550] = "Appears after To Sow the Seed. The children hide at 51.4, 41.5 (up between the trees), 51.7, 39.5, 50.4, 40.8 and 49.5, 43.1 (behind trees).",
    [91558] = "Lady Darkglen is at 35.9, 48.3; she only shows on the minimap when you're close.",
    [91559] = "The drops are rare, and the pools hurt over time.",
    [91560] = "Do Calculated Culling first (it's given at the same time); until then the scouts can't be cured. Leaving and coming back also helps. The scouts don't show on the minimap.",
    [91561] = "The area's debuff clears once you're far enough away.",
    [91565] = "Alliance version: starts with Amari Lyndon at 40.8, 84.0 in Slayer's Rise. Entirely PvE, ending in the Voidscar Arena dungeon; War Mode can stay off. Needs level 88.",
    [91566] = "Horde version: starts with Dar'gul at 34.9, 80.2 in Slayer's Rise (the in-game map wrongly shows the flight master). PvE only; needs level 88.",
    [91589] = "If the food vanishes as you approach, finish the campaign up to Seeds of the Rift first. The ribs are on the grass left of the table.",
    [91603] = "If the turn-in NPC is missing, take and finish the second domanaar's quest at the arena entrance (53, 25).",
    [91605] = "Do Voidscar Arena: Two Against One as well, or the domanaar won't be at the turn-in.",
    [91694] = "All PvE: you don't need any PvP quests for Sojourner of Voidstorm.",
    [91822] = "Lor'themar is in the Silvermoon City harbor, at 33.4, 36.2.",
    [91826] = "A demanding puzzle; the box is right next to her at 61, 68.",
    [91827] = "After the main campaign moves on, Lor'themar may lose the turn-in marker; players report it as a bug.",
    [91828] = "Needs level 90 and No Loose Ends; Valeera then offers it in the Bazaar.",
    [91831] = "Press all four pylons rather than freeing prisoners. In a group it can fail: do it solo.",
    [91833] = "Starts with Vun'zarah at 38, 22 and seems to need level 90.",
    [91835] = "If the marker points into the ground, hand it in to Dak'zor at 44.9, 36.5.",
    [91838] = "The last orb is in the cave to the north, at 46.5, 37.6.",
    [91840] = "If she's missing or stuck at 1 health, toggle War Mode in a capital and come back.",
    [91872] = "Opens after the One Does Not Simply Walk Into Harandar achievement (the zone story); A Goblin in Harandar and Bloomtown need it too.",
    [91873] = "There are no waves: go out and kill the hostile enemies in the area.",
    [91874] = "Just fly close to a fire on your mount; it goes out by itself.",
    [91876] = "Click the faint outlined spots on the tree behind her and on the vines in a circle around her.",
    [91885] = "Kill enemies nearby, then click the icon; the voidwalker drains the energy for you.",
    [91918] = "Needs level 90 and No Loose Ends; pick it up from Valeera in the Bazaar.",
    [91958] = "Zul'jarra waits at the Den of Nalorakk entrance (the bear's open mouth) at 31.5, 83.9. Normal difficulty is fine, a follower group works too. Dismount and leave bear or travel form to place the offerings.",
    [92021] = "Picked up around 37, 72 near Windrunner Spire; the quest giver appears once you're far enough in the campaign.",
    [92022] = "Elder Mournbats drop the venom far more reliably than Venomous Mournbats.",
    [92024] = "The last clue is the book on the bed.",
    [92025] = "She's in the open-world Windrunner Spire a short flight away; don't queue the dungeon.",
    [92061] = "Needs level 86 to appear.",
    [92156] = "Use the Consuming Brand from your bags (or beside the quest) on Shadowguard corpses; the extra action button isn't what gives progress.",
    [92163] = "Appears after Den of Nalorakk: Unforgiven.",
    [92165] = "No need to fish: the skewers are lying next to the huts.",
    [92390] = "The quest giver is in Slayer's Rise, at 39.8, 84.2.",
    [92396] = "Starts outside Silvermoon's main gates with Terel Bloodfate at 50.1, 34.2, even though the map shows it inside the city. Turn on low-level quests if you can't see it.",
    [92398] = "The quest giver is at 50.2, 34.2, outside the city gates.",
    [92451] = "Stand right next to Ani for the button to show up.",
    [92452] = "The trinkets are small and lie next to the murlocs: 47.5, 63.5, 46.0, 62.0 and 45.3, 61.1.",
    [92496] = "Go right as you enter; a barrier blocks the left side.",
    [92505] = "Time-gated: Leona Darkstrider only appears later in the story. Once available she's sparring at 53.2, 70.4.",
    [92506] = "The targets are shared by everyone and respawn slowly; expect to wait at busy times.",
    [92507] = "Leona can take a while to appear.",
    [92508] = "Don't take the portal to Silvermoon: go to 31, 52 in Voidstorm.",
    [92509] = "The talon drops rarely and Ultradons spawn slowly; it can take many kills.",
    [92510] = "Umbric only appears once the campaign has unlocked this base.",
    [92512] = "If Princeps Ravenor doesn't appear after you talk to Leona, drop the quest and take it again.",
    [92520] = "Survivors: Calia Menethil 47.9, 61.7, Moira Thaurissan 51.3, 62.9, Tahu Sagewind 35.5, 45.2, High Prelate Rata 41.2, 57.6. Collect them all before the three named ones, or the last disappears.",
    [92531] = "If the Loa of Medicine can't be selected, deselect your main Loa, close the window and open it again.",
    [92607] = "The shade does respawn at the marked spot, after about a minute with no corpse left behind.",
    [92617] = "These are the bigger enemies around the pit, not inside the Grudge Pit delve.",
    [92657] = "Appears only after the Voidstorm campaign. If you take the Stormarion Citadel quests (such as Tactical Acquisition) first, Lysikas disappears until you abandon them.",
    [92662] = "Aim at their feet.",
    [92689] = "Aethas Sunreaver's part completes by itself after you do Vereesa's The Silversun Compact. If Rommath isn't outside the entrance, abandon and retake the quest.",
    [92694] = "Starts at 70.5, 51.2. Each character needs it done to choose the last relic, even if your warband already finished it.",
    [92695] = "If the turn-in marker is wrong, it's at 72.4, 55.7. Hunters: a few unique pets can be tamed only during this quest.",
    [92696] = "For the uprooting, run away from the vine while it's attached; don't do it in a druid flight or travel form. Turn it in at 72.4, 55.7.",
    [92697] = "Move the feather onto each gold dot with the arrows without reusing a path. Alt+Z hides your UI if it covers the board. A reported solution: board 1: 2,3,2,4,2,2,3,2,2,4,4; board 2: 3,1,3,1,4,4,4,1,4,4,2,3,2,3,2,2,4,2,2,3,1,3,3,3,3; board 3: 3,3,1,4,1,4,4,2,4,2,2,3,3,2,2,2,2,2.",
    [92728] = "The map marker is wrong: it's at 35.4, 57.6.",
    [92732] = "Opens after the Harandar zone story (One Does Not Simply Walk Into Harandar); progress in Arator's Journey can also unlock it.",
    [92736] = "The turn-in marker is wrong: hand it in where you took it, at 41.6, 67.4.",
    [92739] = "The map's end point is wrong: he's at 31.4, 65.0, just inside the wide end of the horn-shaped structure.",
    [92865] = "Dismount for the feeding button to appear. If F'liks is hard to hit, talk to him so he stands still.",
    [92866] = "Pick them all up and you'll be shown where to go next; the enemies that spawn don't need killing.",
    [92883] = "The Tail Spores lie on the ground near the trees as small highlighted objects; the flying Sporegliders don't drop them.",
    [92884] = "The Tail Spore is on top of the twisted vine near Al'yaat, between a rock and a lamp post.",
    [92885] = "Talk to Ketan before killing Radooni, or it won't count and you'll wait for the respawn.",
    [92895] = "The lead-in can also be taken from the Adventure Guide, under Legacy of the Amani.",
    [92897] = "If it isn't offered, accept it from the Adventure Guide under Legacy of the Amani (bottom right).",
    [92900] = "Zul'jan is just outside the Den's waterfall exit, not in the hut above.",
    [92931] = "Use Cauterize from your bags while targeting Zul'jarra. To talk to Dok'zor, first knock out the training dummy he's fighting.",
    [92934] = "Stand up before you start (sitting blocks the heals). If the quest givers vanish after you leave the vision, ask Orweyna in the temple behind them to start it again.",
    [92935] = "Don't leave the vehicle: the turn-in NPCs are only in that phase.",
    [92936] = "If the extra action button is hidden, macro /click ExtraActionButton1 and press it in the circle.",
    [92951] = "The scrolls are outside the dungeon, not inside.",
    [92953] = "Use the Necromantic Interrogation action button on each corpse; it works after Digging Deeper's scrolls are collected.",
    [92954] = "There's now a dialogue option to skip the dungeon and complete this instantly. If you run it: loot the second boss for the notes and kill the last boss; Follower Dungeons work, Mythic+ doesn't let you loot the notes.",
    [93022] = "If the turn-in NPC vanished, go back to where you picked it up, at 47.1, 31.3.",
    [93023] = "If the turn-in NPC doesn't show after the furies, fly to Tokka's Landing and back; she appears at the top of the stairs.",
    [93093] = "Nothing leads you here: the quest giver just appears on the map.",
    [93094] = "One of the six is in a cave with a hard-to-see entrance at 28.6, 35.3.",
    [93095] = "If you looted the tusk while someone else fought the Tusk Taker and he won't come back, abandon and retake the quest.",
    [93096] = "If Kel'vujo isn't there yet, wait a minute.",
    [93178] = "Won't work while your zone campaign quest is active. The child on the wall is at 38.5, 26.6.",
    [93179] = "Don't mount up or the child stops following. The pool is at 51.5, 32.8.",
    [93180] = "She moves after you accept it: meet her at 51.5, 30.6.",
    [93182] = "If nobody is at the hut to take it, relog; the NPCs sometimes fail to appear.",
    [93233] = "Pat the tiny Curious Murpholes, don't kill them.",
    [93257] = "The quest giver waits on a dock by the river south of the village, at 45.9, 70.7.",
    [93339] = "Only some murlocs drop the trinkets (the ones riding turtles are a good bet); more lie on the ground under the murloc tents on the bridge.",
    [93389] = "The last item is a leather band on the beach at 62.4, 30.7.",
    [93390] = "Needs Unusual Alchemy done first. If the NPC gets stuck when you're done, relog.",
    [93393] = "If nothing happens at Friend Delivered (broken egg, idle elemental), abandon and redo it.",
    [93417] = "Before queuing, go underground to the dungeon entrance (way down at 43, 44; the city is at 41, 44) to check on the troops; running the dungeon first doesn't count for that step.",
    [93418] = "Meet the NPCs outside the Gate of the Serpent's Eye, entering the underground from the north, before you run the raid, or it won't count that week. In Story Mode, keep the follow button on so the followers keep up.",
    [93419] = "The dagger sticks out of the ground about ten yards in front of Zul'jarra: click it to heal her, then click it again to destroy it.",
    [93420] = "If Lor'themar has the marker but nothing happens, leave your raid group.",
    [93433] = "If the Elder isn't at the marker, relog there.",
    [93435] = "If Zungam is out of place and evading, toggle War Mode in a capital and come back.",
    [93437] = "The Lynx Loa is the quickest form for this one.",
    [93440] = "Needs De Legend of de Hash'ey and Broken Bridges done first.",
    [93801] = "Picked up from Scout Philanas near Shadowguard Point (34, 44); hand it in to Lady Darkglen at 34.6, 43.8.",
    [93841] = "A short chain of five quests; finishing it opens the Ki'clak Snack Attack world quest.",
    [93849] = "If no Collected Ectoplasm appears, abandon and retake the quest.",
    [94031] = "The ribcage is outside the ship: facing the entrance, walk along the hull's right side; it's on the ground.",
    [94040] = "If the bones and meat at Tooth o' Sargoth can't be clicked, abandon and pick the quest up again.",
    [94370] = "Can't be picked up if you already did Not What I Ordered; that's fine, the storyline still counts.",
    [94388] = "A lead-in to Theft Tracking. If it seems stuck, check for Reenact the Crime in your log and use the Arcane Timepiece at the West Sanctum.",
    [94396] = "Can't be picked up if you've done Spellbook Scuffle; the storyline still counts.",
    [94527] = "If there's no survival bar and your shell takes no damage, leave and come back in.",
    [94531] = "Lor'themar only takes it after you finish the whole Season 1 story (The War of Light and Shadow).",
    [94677] = "Loot the three musings in order: a chest at 31.0, 64.7, then scrolls at 33.0, 65.1 and 30.5, 67.5. The later ones take a minute or so to appear.",
    [94941] = "If Hiss'mir gives no credit, drop the quest and take it again.",
    [94957] = "Party sync with a level 80 character can make it appear if Liadrin offers nothing.",
    [94967] = "Use the quest interaction, don't just buy the item from the vendor. Every Frayed ghost in the Ring of Glory area can drop what you need; if they show as friendly, fly away and back.",
    [95008] = "Do the introduction on every character: the free reagent bag only comes from this chain.",
    [95324] = "Elder Hagar disappears if you take the next campaign quest first. Hand that one in and she comes back.",
    [95521] = "Starts from a small Faintly Glowing Gem on fallen pillar stones in the water by a skeleton, at the bottom of the stairs (48.0, 51.9).",
    [95522] = "Leave your raid group before using the statue.",
    [95523] = "After each kill, click the blue orb that appears next to the body (it doesn't go to your bags). Stand in melee range so it drops.",
    [95524] = "If Gal'fon's bow isn't there after clicking his statue, relog; it leans against the wall to his right.",
    [95973] = "If Lor'themar doesn't offer it, accept The Call of the Void from Suggested Content in the Adventure Guide.",
    [96090] = "Needs A Bond of Brothers in your log first, or nothing drops. If they still drop nothing, go to the green waterfall at 53.3, 45.9 north of the small central island.",
    [96091] = "Stand at the top of the wooden stairs for the extra button, then keep each of the three markers inside its two lines. When balanced, wait a few seconds rather than pressing again.",
    [96093] = "No need to finish the delve: enter on Tier 1, go to the marked spot, then leave.",
    [96099] = "Finishing it lets you buy a decor piece from the Decor Specialist at 58.6, 45.9 for Voidlight Marl.",
    [96110] = "Opens during the Original Sin step of The Curse of Ula'tek (step 4 of 6). Fish in the venomous ooze, not water: the ooze waterfall at 50.9, 64.7 works well.",
    [96111] = "Not inside the delve: fly around the bases of large trees for the wood piles (one was at 61.0, 83.5 on Gnarldor Isle).",
    [96112] = "Unlocks at the Cursed Angler rank with Captain Tokka.",
    [96113] = "Unlocks at Captain Tokka's 4th reputation rank. Fish at 51, 53 in the Vault, then take the Black-Venom Grouper to the island up north at 63.9, 8.4; the canoe arrives once it's placed.",
    [96439] = "If the scouts aren't there, come back a little later; they appear after a while.",
    [96450] = "If the Missive from Malacrass isn't on the boxes on the right, wait about five minutes for it to respawn.",
    [96469] = "Read the tablet on the wall for the order, then click the altar items: charm, mortar and pestle, urn, bones.",
    [96471] = "If it doesn't complete, step out of the cave and wait a moment.",
    [96523] = "Starts with Kehiah at 59.4, 50.9, above ground.",
    [96539] = "If you disconnect mid-quest and come back phased out, drop the quest and go back to Kehiah.",
    [96544] = "If too few dragonhawks spawn, abandon and retake the quest.",
    [96545] = "To return to the story after leaving, tell Kehiah at 59.4, 50.9 that you're ready to listen.",
}
